{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of R14 retirement 2 of 2, the legacy GitHub demo context and the fixed demo origins, with planner amendment 999ffe93. The head is 1e5cfe21e507759db5d95fc9151751f0e9158e12 (tree 137a81791603dcdd092aa599d8c3b764401899a6), for request fe2305a2, under builder promise ab7e2c41. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read the implementation note 813b6c56 first. Then I read the request, the amendment and the R14 decisions 3240b82d. Then I read every change from Main c7c51714.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- Base and delta. The head descends from Main c7c51714 through 5 commits. They change exactly the 21 paths named by the 21 artifacts, one artifact per path. None of the artifacts has been superseded. The worktree was clean at the head.\n- First gate. The first gate at d01ed5b0 exited 2 in 0.3 s, at the whitespace step, before any compiler or test stage. It remains failed.\n- Repair. From d01ed5b0 to b9cd8f45 the only change is one final blank line removed from packages/scope/src/demo-creation.ts. The retained patch shows the same.\n- Final gate. The full ordinary gate at b9cd8f45 (tree b7c088a8) exited 0, with the source unchanged before and after. Its output ends \"gate passed\". This is a passing gate, so no follow-up exception is needed. From b9cd8f45 to the head, only the note and its manifest change.\n- Evidence:\n  - The committed manifest has SHA-256 326a7cdb…. All 105 entries match their recorded size and hash, and no entry is writable.\n  - SHA256SUMS has 104 lines, all OK.\n  - The report tail's SHA256SUMS has SHA-256 7ff4ee45…, as stated. Its 31 lines are all OK, it holds 32 files, and none is writable.\n- Proxy run. The local proxy run at d01ed5b0 exited 0. Its source differs from the gate source only by that blank line. Its result records:\n  - configured create 201;\n  - unset, forwarded-only and wrong-service creates 403;\n  - a different Host accepted;\n  - two MCP sessions with two room tool calls;\n  - rotation 200 and retirement 200;\n  - 7 journals verified;\n  - health 200 with sessions `ok` and register `ready`.\n- The request's witnesses:\n  - `git grep workers.dev` finds nothing in packages/scope/src/demo-creation.ts or apps/room/demo-creation.ts.\n  - The demo-offer tests pass with the current configuration.\n  - The new cases show that an origin the setting does not name gets 404 before any namespace lookup. This holds for a wrong origin, a malformed `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` and forwarded headers alone.\n  - No `legacyGitHubDemo` or `LEGACY_ORIGINS` remains outside notes.\n- Action pins. `git ls-remote` on the official repositories gives these results:\n  - actions/checkout `v6` and `v6.1.0` are d23441a4…;\n  - actions/setup-node `v6` and `v6.5.0` are 24997072….\n\n  These are the pinned commits.\n- Documents:\n  - check-doc-links on an export of the head: 723 links, 0 broken.\n  - check-notes c7c51714..1e5cfe21: 0 warnings.\n  - check-commit-messages: 5 checked, 0 flagged.\n  - `git diff --check`: clean.\n\nI reran no suite and no proxy.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe request's work is done as asked:\n- `LegacyGitHubDemoContext`, `legacyGitHubDemoConfig`, `LegacyGitHubDemoSettings`, the legacy origin set and `ORIGIN` are removed.\n- The route's fixed-origin branch is removed.\n- The route now has one path. It reads the deployment's `DEMO_START_CONFIG`, compares the effective public origin (H1's `readPublicOrigin`) with the configured origin, and checks any selected reference against the configured register.\n- The setting keeps its wire version 3. It becomes the same internal version 2 context, and the public offer stays version 2.\n- The configured origin is checked by the same canonical-origin rule as `PUBLIC_ORIGIN`.\n\nRemoving `legacyGitHubDemoConfig` also removes its other caller, the extra GitHub host roots in github-wiring.ts. That wiring is now bound only by `hostBound` on the register that `GITHUB_APP_CONFIG` pins. `GitHubBindings` no longer extends `DemoCreationBindings`. The worker's GitHub wiring key no longer includes `DEMO_START_CONFIG` or `DEPLOYMENT`, and `Env` takes `DemoCreationBindings` directly. The client's version 1 offer decoder, the historical definitions and the pins are unchanged.\n\nAmendment 999ffe93:\n1. Name. The celld project is now `dap-celld-local`; its bindings, migrations and vars are otherwise identical. The `entryIdentity` logic is gone. Each Worker name now binds its literal entry, and the import walk checks every file with the same tracked-and-not-symlinked rule. docs/security/settings.md gives `dap-celld-local` its own deployment row and adds it to every room setting row. docs/celld.md and the proxy driver follow, and the proxy run passed with the new name.\n2. Workflow pins. Both workflow steps are pinned to full commit hashes with `# v6` comments. docs/testing.md states the rule in one sentence next to the smoke description.\n\n## Security\n\n- The change removes authority and adds none. A legacy version 1 or 2 setting, a fixed origin or an exact retained reference no longer produces an offer. The tests show 404 with no namespace lookup for the retired references. A demo setting no longer adds GitHub host roots, and the tests show `accepts` false and `send` null for those roots. Ordinary GitHub binding is unchanged, and the test keeps `accepts(REGISTER, …)` true.\n- Origin identity still comes only from `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` or the request URL, never from forwarded headers. A wrong or malformed identity refuses before lookup.\n- The configured origin can now be any canonical HTTPS or loopback origin; before, only the one fixed origin was allowed. This is operator configuration, and the route still requires an exact match with the effective request origin. This is what the request asked for.\n\nDeployment note for the planner. This is not a defect.\n- dap-demo. Its current setting is version 3 with origin `https://dap-demo.inguz.workers.dev`, and that form is still accepted. The note correctly lists no setting change. After the deploy, check that `GET /v1/demo/creation-offer` on dap-demo still answers 200.\n- artroom-scope. At c7c51714, docs/deploy.md said that retained Start requests on artroom-scope end on 8 November 2026. With this source, they end when artroom-scope is next deployed. The head updates docs/deploy.md to say so, and keeps the 8 November cleanup of the setting and the unused secrets. The extra GitHub roots were already inactive there: the planner's record says `GITHUB_APP_CONFIG` was deleted from that Worker on 2026-10-19, and `outsideOf` selects GitHub wiring only when it is set. I have not read the deployed settings. R14 decision 2 retires this context, so I take the earlier end date as intended. If it is not, hold the artroom-scope deploy until 8 November.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThis is a net removal in production: the legacy decoder, the version 1 offer branch, the two extra roots and the shim-identity logic are gone, about 80 lines. The settings rows grow by one name each, which the amendment chose. I see nothing to cut.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved. Server-side legacy offers and the extra GitHub roots are removed. Origin identity comes only from configuration or the request URL. Ordinary GitHub binding and the retained client decoding are unchanged.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- Request conditions:\n  - one head;\n  - ordinary gate passed at b9cd8f45 (the earlier failed gate is kept as failed);\n  - the grep and refusal witnesses hold;\n  - no setting change is listed;\n  - public wording names no other product;\n  - order: after retirement 1 (c7c51714), before 7ee9a63b.\n- Amendment 999ffe93: both items are done.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing. The dap-demo deploy is the planner's, after landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:813b6c56fb32d6a16bdd7437ce3f63784fc35efb","binding":"assigned","head":"1e5cfe21e507759db5d95fc9151751f0e9158e12","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cc37736a15e34f202d64218ec0aa5ff2b3d2e1a7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ab7e2c4168ebaac6a807e50c8e11e3859a75e8d3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cc37736a15e34f202d64218ec0aa5ff2b3d2e1a7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}